From 8440f25036c0861448507186d0eea9caf240fd5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:52:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WU-B13h: callers carry the frame epoch to the supplied-epoch
 writers

Ordered after WU-B13 slice g. Base rule as WU-B13: applies after
StegVerse-Labs/.github #3241, #3263, #3230 and #3207 merge, on top of
slices a-g. Three caller transitions the supplied-HB-epoch slices leave red:

1. Claim-allocator workflow: both consume steps supply --hb-epoch from the
   receipt-chain frame epoch, the epoch the verified Organization ledger HEAD
   records (new scripts/organization_ledger_head_epoch.py, reusing the
   consumer's ledger_custody/verify_organization_chain and the kernel's
   supplied_epoch_failure). A HEAD without a supplied epoch, or with a
   clock-derived one, is refused six-field FAIL_CLOSED; nothing is consumed.
   The tests that forbade the --hb-epoch string are narrowed to their intent:
   no date/time source feeds the epoch, and only the ledger-derived epoch is
   accepted. New tests: reproducing (red on the #3241 workflow), clock-derived
   epochs still rejected, helper refusals.
2. scripts/dispatch_resident_execution_requests.py: dispatch(hb_epoch=) and
   --hb-epoch carry the frame epoch to the component-011 observation
   (aggregate_transition(hb_epoch=)) and to the claim-allocator consumer.
   A missing or invalid epoch is six-field FAIL_CLOSED before any append.
   The 6 group-A tests the fixture cannot reach supply the epoch.
3. kernel.dispatch: the capability-address operation is handed the carrier
   frame's epoch (carrier_epoch), and a frame without a supplied one is
   refused CarrierEpochRefusal (six fields) before the operation runs.

No clock reads in runtime code. Stdlib only, no new dependencies.

Evidence class: SOURCE_IMPLEMENTED, validation pending.

